bin/ is for command line scripts that should be included in the $PATH.

Scripts
-------

**plotnightobs** : Create a graphical timeline of observations and calculate basic summary statistics

**plottimeobs** : Generate a detailed graphical timeline of activity between two time intervals

**plotobsefficiency** : Generate a summary plot of observing efficiency across many nights

**updateefficiency** : Update table of observing efficiency data

Tertiary webpage updates
------------------------

`tertiary-status-update.cronjob` runs `run-status-update.sh` at 17:30 and
19:30 UTC. Each launch submits a CPU worker and one conditional retry for the
programs listed in `tertiary-progress.txt`. Slurm serializes these updates.
The launcher log (`bin/status-update-JOBID.out`) records both job IDs.

The worker renders the HTML and requested QA products in a staging directory
beside the live page. It checks the footer, installs the finished products,
and replaces the page last. A subsequent attempt cleans up interrupted staging
files. The worker reports success only after seeing a fresh, complete page.

If the worker fails or times out, Slurm releases the retry. After a successful
first attempt Slurm cancels the unused retry. If both attempts fail, the next
scheduled update starts a new pair. Inspect `bin/status-worker-JOBID.out` and
`sacct -j FIRST_ID,RETRY_ID --format=JobID,State,Elapsed,ExitCode,MaxRSS`.

